On Sun, 5 Dec 2004, Tyson Whitehead wrote:

> Does anyone have some advice about what type of USB PCI card to get (so I can
> expect it to work under Debian on a PWS500au).  I recall someone saying a
> while ago that USB under Alpha was not so well supported?

USB works fine for me on a 433au GL2 Miata.

Miata SRM doesnt support USB though and will auto switch to serial 
console if you dont have a PS/2 keyboard plugged in. But how often do 
you need to tinker with SRM? ;) Linux 2.6.8 image has no problems..

The XP1000 SRM might support USB keyboard (but you have to enable it 
with an env var AFAIK).

